FreePhish Detection — Enhanced Features, GAN Adversarial Evaluation, and DE Feature Weighting

Re-implementation and extension of FreePhish (Saha Roy et al., 2023), a phishing-detection system targeting pages hosted on Free Website Building (FWB) services. This project extends the original 22-feature StackModel with a richer feature set, evaluates its robustness against a GAN-based adversarial attack, and explores Differential Evolution (DE) as an alternative feature-weighting approach.

See samplepaper.tex (or the compiled PDF) for the full write-up: literature review, methodology, and experimental results.

What's in this repo
Scripts
File	Purpose
freephish_old.py	Baseline: trains the original 22-feature StackModel (train), compares two result files (compare), and runs live classification (monitor, analyze).
freephish_enhanced.py	Trains the enhanced StackModel on a 100-feature set (URL, HTML, FWB-specific, brand, behavioral) (train).
freephish_gan.py	GAN-based adversarial evaluation: generates adversarial phishing pages and evaluates both models under attack (adv), retrains the enhanced model on GAN-augmented data (retrain), and tunes the attack budget/epochs via grid search before retraining (tune).
freephish_de.py	Differential Evolution search over per-feature weights on the enhanced feature space (train).
freephish_classify_all.py	Loads any subset of the four trained models and classifies a shared list of live URLs with each one side by side — no training, inference only.
requirements.txt	Python dependencies.
Notebooks (Google Colab)
File	Purpose
FreePhish_pipeline_complete.ipynb	Full training pipeline: downloads the dataset, trains the baseline and enhanced models, runs the GAN attack/adversarial-training experiments, runs DE, and downloads all four trained .joblib model files. Run this once beforehand — not during a live demo.
freephish_classify_all_colab.ipynb	The live demo notebook: upload the four trained models, fetch a handful of real phishing/benign URLs, and classify them side by side. Inference only, runs in seconds.
Trained models (if included)

model.joblib (baseline), model_enh.joblib (enhanced), model_adv.joblib (adversarially-trained enhanced), model_de.joblib (DE-weighted enhanced).

How to reproduce
Open FreePhish_pipeline_complete.ipynb in Google Colab.
Upload the five .py scripts and requirements.txt when prompted.
Run all cells top to bottom. This downloads the dataset, trains all four models, and ends by downloading the four .joblib files to your computer.
How to run the live demo
Open freephish_classify_all_colab.ipynb in Google Colab.
Upload the five .py scripts and the four .joblib model files from the step above.
Run all cells. It fetches a set of real phishing (PhishTank) and benign (GitHub Pages) URLs, classifies them with every model you uploaded, and prints a side-by-side comparison table.
Dataset

Sampled from the phreshphish dataset. Not included in this repo — re-download it using the download command in freephish_old.py if you need to retrain from scratch.

Author

Samprita Adhikari — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Kharagpur.
